<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 100.50 from 100.25, the Bundesbank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the Series 123 4-1/2 percent paper to 4.38 percent from 4.44 percent.</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
